      B: { story: 'The 8px grid system is implemented as spacing tokens: --space-1 (4px), --space-2 (8px), --space-3 (12px), --space-4 (16px), --space-6 (24px), --space-8 (32px). Developers know exactly which token to use for which level of spacing. The product becomes measurably more consistent.', lesson: 'The 8px grid is not a design trend — it maps to screen pixel grids and renders crisply on all screen densities. It\'s a foundation, not a constraint.', principle: 'Spacing Tokens', principleDetail: '8px grids are the standard because 8 divides evenly for most screen density multipliers. The system is easy to learn and reduces decision fatigue: every spacing decision has a "right" answer from the token scale.' },
