      B: { story: 'A named type scale is adopted across the product. Existing 14 sizes are audited and each is mapped to its nearest token value. Three unnecessary sizes are eliminated. Typography becomes consistent across all pages — the same spec, everywhere.', lesson: 'A named type scale requires discipline (no more arbitrary sizes) but pays off in consistency, speed, and clarity.', principle: 'Typography Tokens', principleDetail: 'Named type scales are the industry standard: Material Design has 5 display levels + 3 headline + 3 body + 3 label. Polaris has 6 heading levels. The specific levels matter less than their consistency.' },
