      B: { story: 'Four tokens cover all cases: small for chips and tags (4px), medium for cards and buttons (8px), large for modals and panels (16px), full for pill/badge shapes (999px). Every component maps cleanly to one of these. The product feels cohesive.', lesson: 'Semantic radius tokens follow the same principle as semantic colour tokens: the name describes the use, not the value. This makes design decisions immediate — what is this component? Pick the matching radius token.', principle: 'Border Radius Tokens', principleDetail: 'Recommended token set for border radius: sm (small interactive elements: chips, tags, badges), md (standard components: buttons, inputs, cards), lg (large containers: modals, panels, drawers), full (pill shapes, avatar circles).' },
